documentation
elements

	^ 'BlElement is the root of every visual node. Composition is 1:N: an element has at most one parent. Add/remove children with addChild:, addChildren:, addChildFirst:, addChild:at:, removeChild:, removeChildren:, removeChildWithId:; find descendants with childWithId: (id:/elementId: give stable ids). Size and position: size:, extent: (a Point), position:, geometry: (a BlElementGeometry subclass: BlRectangleGeometry, BlRoundedRectangleGeometry, BlCircleGeometry, BlPolygonGeometry, BlStadiumGeometry, ...). Layout: layout: aBlLayout plus constraintsDo: [ :c | c horizontal matchParent; vertical fitContent ] shorthand hMatchParent/vMatchParent/hFitContent/vFitContent/hExact: 100/vExact: 100/matchParent/fitContent, padding:, margin:, minSize:/maxSize:. After changes call requestLayout/forceLayout and react with whenLayoutedDo:. Visibility: visibility: (BlVisibilityVisible/Hidden/Gone), opacity:, zIndex:/elevation:, mouseCursor:, effect: (shadows, blurs, clipping), compositingMode:.'